{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f2c1d3e-9a4b-4c5d-8e6f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
    "name": "Chronicle ThreatGraph",
    "description": "API for **Chronicle**: submit threat-report URLs or PDFs and poll the resulting knowledge graph / STIX 2.1-lite bundle.\n\n## Base URL\n`{{baseUrl}}` defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:3210` (override in the environment).\n\n## Authentication\nAll endpoints use `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (set at collection level via `{{apiToken}}`). Auth is only enforced when the server sets `CHRONICLE_API_TOKEN`. Without a token:\n- non-production: requests pass through unauthenticated\n- production with no token configured: **503** `Server authentication is not configured.`\n- wrong/missing token: **401** `A valid bearer token is required.`\n\n## Processing lifecycle\n`queued → ingesting → extracting → modeling → done` (or `failed`).\n\n## Limits\n- Max report size: **10 MB** (`MAX_REPORT_BYTES`); oversized → **413**.\n- Only `application/pdf` uploads accepted → else **415**.\n- Graph caps: ≤ 250 entities, ≤ 500 relationships.\n\n## Error format (RFC 7807 problem+json)\n```json\n{\"type\": \"https://chronicle.local/problems/validation-error\", \"title\": \"Request rejected\", \"status\": 400, \"detail\": \"...\"}\n```\nKnown `type` URIs: `problems/validation-error` (400), `problems/unauthorized` (401), `problems/not-found` (404), `problems/not-ready` (409), `problems/internal-error` (500).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:3210",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "report_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "job_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{apiToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Reports",
      "description": "Create and poll reports. Each accepted submission returns **202** with `report_id` (= `job_id`); processing runs in the background.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create report from URL",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/threat-report\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "reports"]
            },
            "description": "Submit a threat-report **URL** as JSON.\n\nBody: `{\"url\": \"<valid https? URL>\"}`\n\nReturns **202 Accepted** with `report_id`, `job_id` (same value) and `status` (`queued`). Processing continues asynchronously.\n\nErrors:\n- **400** invalid JSON, or `url` missing/not a valid URL (`Provide a valid report URL.`)\n- **401** missing/bad bearer token\n- **413** body larger than the 10 MB limit\n- **415** wrong content type\n\nThe test script captures `report_id`/`job_id` into collection variables for the polling requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.report_id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('report_id', body.report_id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', body.job_id ?? body.report_id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "202 Accepted",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports",
                "header": [
                  {
