        {
          "name": "Upload PDF report",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "/path/to/report.pdf"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "reports"]
            },
            "description": "Upload a **PDF** threat report as `multipart/form-data`.\n\nForm field: `file` (the PDF).\n\nReturns **202 Accepted** with `report_id`, `job_id` and `status` (`queued`).\n\nErrors:\n- **400** missing `file` field or malformed multipart body\n- **401** missing/bad bearer token\n- **413** file is empty or larger than the 10 MB limit (`The PDF exceeds the configured size limit.`)\n- **415** file content-type is not `application/pdf` (`Only PDF uploads are accepted.`)\n\nThe test script captures `report_id`/`job_id` into collection variables."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.report_id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('report_id', body.report_id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', body.job_id ?? body.report_id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "202 Accepted",
