        {
          "name": "Get report STIX bundle",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/{{report_id}}/stix",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "reports", "{{report_id}}", "stix"]
            },
            "description": "STIX 2.1-lite bundle for a finished report, as a JSON download (`content-disposition: attachment; filename=chronicle-<id>.stix.json`).\n\nReturns **200** with a STIX bundle:\n- `{ \"type\": \"bundle\", \"id\": \"bundle--<uuid>\", \"spec_version\": \"2.1\", \"objects\": [...] }`\n- `objects[]` = entities mapped to STIX types (`threat-actor`, `malware`, `tool`, `vulnerability`, `indicator`, `campaign`, `identity`) with `id`, `created`, `modified`, `name`, `confidence` (0-100), `labels` (the internal entity type), `x_chronicle_report_id`\n- plus `relationship` objects linking `source_ref` → `target_ref` with `relationship_type`\n\nErrors:\n- **404** unknown `report_id`\n- **409** bundle not ready yet (`The STIX bundle is not ready yet.`)"
          },
          "response": [
